.TH SDL_clamp 3 "SDL 3.5.0" "Simple Directmedia Layer" "SDL3 FUNCTIONS"
.SH NAME
SDL_clamp \- Return a value clamped to a range.
.SH SYNOPSIS
.nf
.B #include <SDL3/SDL_stdinc.h>
.PP
.BI "#define SDL_clamp(x, a, b) (((x) < (a)) ? (a) : (((x) > (b)) ? (b) : (x)))
.fi
.SH DESCRIPTION
If
.BR x
is outside the range a values between
.BR a
and
.BR b ,
the returned value will be
.BR a
or
.BR b
as appropriate\[char46] Otherwise,
.BR x
is returned\[char46]
.PP
This macro will produce incorrect results if
.BR b
is less than
.BR a \[char46]
.PP
This is a helper macro that might be more clear than writing out the comparisons directly, and works with any type that can be compared with the
.BR <
and
.BR >
operators\[char46] However, it double-evaluates all its parameters, so do not use expressions with side-effects here\[char46]

.SH MACRO PARAMETERS
.TP
.I x
the value to compare\[char46]
.TP
.I a
the low end value\[char46]
.TP
.I b
the high end value\[char46]
.SH RETURN VALUE
Returns x, clamped between a and b\[char46]

.SH THREAD SAFETY
It is safe to call this macro from any thread\[char46]

.SH AVAILABILITY
This macro is available since SDL 3\[char46]2\[char46]0\[char46]

